WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.940
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs & Migoto

01:35.040 --> 01:39.990
Episode 24:
Love Torn Apart

01:48.210 --> 01:49.570
Arthur!

01:49.840 --> 01:51.320
Arthur!

01:52.870 --> 01:54.160
Arthur!

01:55.700 --> 01:57.780
What happened, mother?

01:58.050 --> 01:58.930
Arthur...

02:00.570 --> 02:04.190
You'll be glad, we finally found where Remy is.

02:04.210 --> 02:05.730
Really?

02:06.520 --> 02:09.460
She's living at a place with a man named Gaspard.

02:09.800 --> 02:12.630
When Mary visited he said she wasn't there.

02:12.650 --> 02:15.740
But she wrote in her letter that she'll certainly bring her back.

02:19.730 --> 02:22.860
Mother, let's go to Paris to meet her and pick her up.

02:23.820 --> 02:26.000
But...

02:26.350 --> 02:29.820
Don't worry about me. I'm totally fine.

02:29.860 --> 02:31.750
If I see Remy, I'll be even better.

02:32.760 --> 02:36.850
If my father were alive, he would've done it.

02:40.940 --> 02:41.810
Mother!

02:50.790 --> 02:51.950
All right.

02:52.700 --> 02:54.220
Arthur...

03:06.790 --> 03:09.580
Miss Mary, what you've been worried about has come true.

03:10.280 --> 03:14.840
That guy, Gaspard, has a really bad reputation.

03:15.320 --> 03:18.840
Even when first meeting him, I had a bad feeling.

03:20.380 --> 03:25.160
He forces kids who don't have any parents or were sold to pay off debt to work

03:25.180 --> 03:26.680
and collects money from them.

03:27.080 --> 03:28.440
Then what about Remy?

03:28.640 --> 03:32.170
She's probably forced to work somewhere.

03:32.490 --> 03:35.370
He told us that he'd let us see Remy,

03:35.480 --> 03:36.690
but we can't trust him.

03:37.830 --> 03:39.790
What should we do?

03:39.900 --> 03:43.710
The Madam and Arthur are coming to Paris soon.

03:44.330 --> 03:47.250
We have to find Remy at all costs before then.

03:47.830 --> 03:48.760
Yes.

03:53.940 --> 03:57.250
The children at Gaspard's house?

03:57.270 --> 04:01.010
Yes, there's a girl named Remy there. Do you have any idea where she is?

04:01.260 --> 04:02.110
Heh!

04:08.260 --> 04:11.110
Please!
- All right, all right.

04:11.120 --> 04:12.480
Excuse me!

04:13.590 --> 04:17.980
We're looking for a girl living at Gaspard's place.

04:19.020 --> 04:20.230
Gaspard's place?

04:20.790 --> 04:22.980
A girl named Remy.

04:23.240 --> 04:27.050
Oh, the girl with the cute monkey, right?

04:27.060 --> 04:29.000
She's a good and cheerful girl.

04:29.930 --> 04:30.990
You know her then?

04:32.660 --> 04:38.640
During this season of the year, Gaspard takes the kids to a village in the countryside

04:38.680 --> 04:40.640
where they do grape picking.

04:41.200 --> 04:43.130
I guess Remy's there, too.

04:43.490 --> 04:45.540
Where is the village?

04:45.570 --> 04:48.800
I believe it's located just south of Paris.

04:49.140 --> 04:51.650
Oh yes, it's Eruville village.

04:53.180 --> 04:55.020
Thank you very much!

04:56.240 --> 05:00.180
Could you tell me anything else about the village?

05:00.510 --> 05:03.650
Keh! She talks too much about something that's none of her business.

05:04.380 --> 05:07.910
I'll never miss a chance to make some good money.

05:16.390 --> 05:18.910
All right! Let's take a break!

05:19.450 --> 05:20.420
Ah...

05:22.530 --> 05:24.740
Finally we can rest!

05:27.090 --> 05:29.270
Ah, I'm so tired!

05:29.290 --> 05:31.750
There's always more no matter how many grapes we pick.

05:32.440 --> 05:34.060
I can't take another step.

05:40.010 --> 05:42.310
It's cold but it feels good.

05:50.120 --> 05:52.130
Joli-Coeur, where are you going?

05:56.470 --> 05:59.040
Joli-Coeur, get down!

06:01.530 --> 06:03.660
You're such a kid!

06:04.790 --> 06:06.590
I'm coming, too!

06:06.810 --> 06:08.720
Wait, Remy!

06:21.260 --> 06:23.690
Where's he gone?

06:25.140 --> 06:26.620
Joli-Coeur!

06:28.420 --> 06:31.490
Get down! Come here, Joli-Coeur!

06:58.030 --> 06:59.910
It's so pretty!

07:50.060 --> 07:51.670
Oh... Remy.

07:52.610 --> 07:54.910
Mattia! Wake up, Mattia!

07:55.240 --> 07:56.460
Hmm?

07:56.790 --> 07:57.960
Come with me!

07:58.480 --> 08:01.750
What? Hey, Remy!
- What?

08:11.150 --> 08:12.960
See, they're beautiful, aren't they?

08:20.490 --> 08:22.040
Nobody will come here.

08:22.470 --> 08:25.280
It'd be okay if you played your violin here.

08:27.060 --> 08:29.740
You'll be a famous musician someday.

08:30.050 --> 08:32.910
You'll definitely be one if you keep practicing.

08:33.820 --> 08:34.660
Remy...

08:52.920 --> 08:55.010
Wow... It looks like a wedding!

08:55.310 --> 08:56.140
Huh?

08:56.350 --> 08:59.150
A wedding for Remy and Mattia!

09:03.240 --> 09:07.060
It's a wedding!
A wedding for Remy and Mattia!

09:08.870 --> 09:10.190
Hey, Lise...

09:10.480 --> 09:14.200
Yeah, it's a wedding!
- Lise, stop it!

09:14.660 --> 09:18.110
Huh? Big brother Mattia's face is turning red.

09:18.130 --> 09:19.300
Lise!

09:21.110 --> 09:23.800
A wedding!
- Stop it, I said!

09:23.820 --> 09:27.500
I'm gonna go tell everybody!
- Hey, Lise!

10:25.570 --> 10:26.980
Huh? That horse cart...

10:27.620 --> 10:29.020
You're late!

10:30.960 --> 10:34.230
As soon as I leave you unsupervised you slack off on the job!

10:36.980 --> 10:38.380
Come on!
- Huh?

10:38.410 --> 10:42.570
Are we going back to Paris? We haven't finished the grape picking yet.

10:42.960 --> 10:44.000
Just Remy!

10:44.660 --> 10:46.080
Why?

10:47.790 --> 10:49.960
Remy!
- Get away!

10:50.790 --> 10:52.040
Mattia!

10:55.400 --> 10:56.080
Remy!

10:57.580 --> 10:58.930
Remy!

11:02.830 --> 11:04.130
Remy!

11:04.190 --> 11:05.140
Remy!

11:07.080 --> 11:09.140
Mattia! Mattia!

11:09.430 --> 11:11.520
Remy! Remy!

11:11.980 --> 11:13.200
Mattia!

11:13.560 --> 11:16.040
Help me!
- Remy!

11:16.200 --> 11:17.020
Remy!

11:17.320 --> 11:19.570
Leave her alone!

11:28.400 --> 11:31.620
I can't believe that one of the kids

11:32.840 --> 11:37.960
living at Gaspard's place is a daughter of the Milligan family.

11:38.120 --> 11:42.970
Not to mention, the Milligan family is one of the greatest pedigree families in England.

11:44.020 --> 11:45.220
Well, now...

11:48.870 --> 11:50.720
Is there a girl called Remy here?

11:55.930 --> 11:58.260
Remy... It's me! Where are you?

12:05.700 --> 12:07.300
Remy's not here.

12:08.690 --> 12:10.830
Boss Gaspard took her away.

12:12.510 --> 12:18.340
What's going on? Did that man pick up Remy to send her to us?

12:19.080 --> 12:23.090
No... He's not that nice of a guy.

12:23.160 --> 12:25.120
He just wants money.

12:25.300 --> 12:27.850
He's probably planning to ransom her.

12:29.610 --> 12:33.530
Then he must've hid Remy from us so we can't find her.

12:33.550 --> 12:35.210
That's probably the case.

12:36.370 --> 12:37.620
Huh... That's horrible.

12:40.020 --> 12:41.240
Big brother Mattia!

12:41.790 --> 12:43.740
How'd it go? Did you find Remy?

12:46.000 --> 12:47.040
No, I didn't.

12:49.820 --> 12:51.700
What about Capi and Joli-Coeur?

12:51.780 --> 12:53.330
Haven't they come back yet?

12:53.910 --> 12:54.540
Tell me...

12:55.100 --> 12:57.570
Remy, what happened to Remy?

12:58.950 --> 13:01.040
Who are you?

13:01.990 --> 13:04.550
We've been looking for Remy.

13:05.170 --> 13:09.050
We finally discovered that she's at Gaspard's place which led us here.

13:09.620 --> 13:11.570
Why are you looking for Remy?

13:12.470 --> 13:16.060
Because Remy is a precious daughter of the Milligan family.

13:19.820 --> 13:21.530
Really?
- Remy is...

13:21.940 --> 13:23.330
Their daughter...

13:27.840 --> 13:30.110
When Remy was just a baby,

13:30.220 --> 13:32.970
she was stolen away by someone.

13:33.000 --> 13:36.080
Since then she's been missing.

13:37.190 --> 13:39.480
We've been looking for her ever since.

13:40.480 --> 13:43.340
We finally found a clue and came here.

13:43.800 --> 13:47.090
How? How would you know that Remy is their daughter?

13:50.630 --> 13:52.850
Does Remy have something like this?

13:53.980 --> 13:57.990
She does! She said that it was given to her by her real mother!

13:59.870 --> 14:03.230
It's proof that Remy is a daughter of the Milligan family.

14:10.600 --> 14:14.370
Where's Gaspard gone anyway?

14:15.280 --> 14:17.680
Mr. Blair, did you find anything?

14:19.390 --> 14:20.660
I see.

14:21.530 --> 14:24.020
Anyway, let's go back to Paris.

14:24.050 --> 14:26.510
There we can list the places that Gaspard might go.

14:26.680 --> 14:28.380
It's all we can do.

14:28.780 --> 14:30.600
Huh... What should we do?

14:30.630 --> 14:33.890
What should I tell the Madam and the boy?

14:49.510 --> 14:52.120
We won't be able to see Remy anymore.

14:52.520 --> 14:54.370
Huh? Why?

14:55.380 --> 14:58.530
Because now she'll know where her real mother is.

14:58.570 --> 15:00.130
Obviously she'll go with her mother.

15:00.520 --> 15:02.160
No, I don't want her to!

15:02.180 --> 15:04.760
I want to stay with Remy forever!

15:09.560 --> 15:10.830
I don't like it either!

15:10.850 --> 15:13.830
Yeah, it'll be boring without Remy.

15:13.870 --> 15:18.190
It can't be helped. Remy's different from what she used to be.

15:18.230 --> 15:19.100
Hey...

16:18.930 --> 16:21.560
Wake up! Hey, Remy!

16:23.180 --> 16:25.060
Why won't you get up!?

16:48.890 --> 16:51.440
You stay here and be quiet for a while!

16:51.910 --> 16:54.630
Why are you doing this!?
- Quit complaining!

16:55.150 --> 16:58.160
Please, send me back to everyone!
- Shut up!

16:58.450 --> 16:59.970
Shut up!

17:00.420 --> 17:04.100
You're an important bargaining chip. I can't send you back.

17:04.110 --> 17:04.800
Huh?

17:05.140 --> 17:06.080
Heh!

17:45.150 --> 17:46.580
What should I do?

17:55.940 --> 17:59.130
Remy wouldn't go!
She wouldn't go anywhere!

18:05.460 --> 18:11.150
She promised we'd be together forever and that we'd never be apart!

18:14.070 --> 18:16.370
<i>Right? Aren't I right?</i>

18:20.500 --> 18:23.600
Oh, did you get it back for me?

18:24.110 --> 18:26.450
I'm so glad.

18:29.590 --> 18:33.550
My real mother gave this to me.

18:33.810 --> 18:36.400
It's my precious treasure.

18:36.420 --> 18:40.900
I feel like I'll be able to meet my mother one day if I keep it.

18:41.760 --> 18:43.310
Thank you, Mattia!

18:44.070 --> 18:47.360
Mother, mother...

18:48.040 --> 18:49.940
So what!

19:20.060 --> 19:21.390
Capi!

19:22.690 --> 19:24.740
Did you find out where Remy is?

19:31.170 --> 19:32.270
Ricardo, I'm going!

19:32.630 --> 19:33.520
Huh?

19:34.630 --> 19:37.040
Gaspard hid Remy!

19:37.100 --> 19:41.060
He's probably planning to ransom money from Remy's mother.

19:41.140 --> 19:43.060
Who knows what terrible things he'll do to Remy

19:43.090 --> 19:45.290
if things don't go the way he wants.

19:46.170 --> 19:47.280
Mattia...

19:48.600 --> 19:50.660
I'll rescue Remy and take her to Paris.

19:50.680 --> 19:52.050
Huh...?

19:53.200 --> 19:55.140
Can you really do that?

19:55.160 --> 19:57.800
But then, we might not be able to see Remy again!

20:01.140 --> 20:04.560
Big brother Mattia, no!

20:07.220 --> 20:10.390
Remy has dreamed of meeting her real mother.

20:13.050 --> 20:15.820
So let's send Remy to her mother.

20:16.330 --> 20:19.630
You want Remy to be happy, right Lise?

20:20.250 --> 20:21.140
Yeah.

20:22.980 --> 20:25.080
I'm sure I'll find Remy.

20:25.720 --> 20:28.180
I'll go too.
- Yeah, me too.

20:28.200 --> 20:31.570
Let's all go together!
- Wait guys!

20:31.990 --> 20:35.390
Let's leave it to Mattia.
We can't waste a second.

20:35.940 --> 20:37.350
We'll leave it to you.

20:48.730 --> 20:50.490
Big brother Mattia!

21:13.270 --> 21:14.660
Mattia!

21:18.150 --> 21:20.720
<i>Remy, hold on, Remy!</i>

21:32.910 --> 21:35.140
Arthur, can't you sleep?

21:35.470 --> 21:38.880
I'm too excited from thinking about seeing Remy tomorrow.

21:38.900 --> 21:40.210
Is that so?

21:41.130 --> 21:50.540
Try to love yourself more

21:50.800 --> 22:00.100
Abandoned dreams can be seen again

22:00.340 --> 22:09.190
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:09.990 --> 22:20.870
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:21.380 --> 22:31.170
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:31.330 --> 22:41.140
From the future that gives us our fate

22:41.200 --> 22:50.510
Try to seek for them more

22:50.800 --> 22:54.610
Give your heart to

22:54.700 --> 23:09.410
That person who is also seeking you

23:18.320 --> 23:22.000
Mattia! Will I ever see Mattia and the rest again?

23:22.600 --> 23:24.380
I'll save you!

23:26.150 --> 23:27.960
I won't let you escape!

23:27.990 --> 23:30.130
Come on, hurry up!
- Okay!

23:32.720 --> 23:36.520
<i>Escape!</i>

23:32.720 --> 23:36.520
Next time:
